  <h6>Credit: Chef John</h6>

  <p>
    “This rotisserie chicken mushroom soup tastes like it simmered for hours, but is easy enough for weeknights thanks to a brilliant shortcut. Creamy, cozy, and packed with flavor, it’s a restaurant-worthy meal at home.”
  </p>

  <h2>Ingredients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>2 tablespoons butter</li>
    <li>8 ounces cremini mushrooms, sliced</li>
    <li>3 garlic cloves, minced</li>
    <li>3 cups chicken bone broth</li>
    <li>1 teaspoon cantanzaro herbs</li>
    <li>1 teaspoon paprika</li>
    <li>1 teaspoon garlic powder</li>
    <li>1 cup heavy cream</li>
    <li>1 cup shredded mozzarella cheese</li>
    <li>1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese</li>
    <li>3 cups cubed or shredded rotisserie chicken</li>
    <li>Chopped fresh parsley</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat.</li>
    <li>Add sliced mushrooms and cook until softened.</li>
    <li>Stir in minced garlic and cook until fragrant.</li>
    <li>Pour in chicken bone broth and bring to a gentle simmer.</li>
    <li>Add cantanzaro herbs, paprika, and garlic powder.</li>
    <li>Stir in heavy cream and continue simmering.</li>
    <li>Add mozzarella and Parmesan, stirring until melted and smooth.</li>
    <li>Mix in shredded rotisserie chicken.</li>
    <li>Simmer until the soup thickens and becomes creamy.</li>
    <li>Top with chopped fresh parsley and serve warm.</li>
  </ol>

